@* Lab adaptation (Sprint 33.9, FE33-049): the BeeDay source injects IStringLocalizer<SharedResources>
   for the two labels and the shared copyright string below — dropped for plain hardcoded English
   strings taken verbatim from SharedResources.en-US.resx at extraction time. *@

@* Sprint 29.4: the public editorial microsite's own layout — used only by the footer's editorial
   page families (About us, Products, Apps, Help, Privacy and terms). Unlike PublicLayout, there is
   no separate PublicHeader: brand + contextual navigation render as part of the page's own colored
   BeeDayHero (InstitutionalPageShell), so header and hero are one surface (§6). AppFooter is
   replaced by the minimal white EditorialFooter (§26). Home, Login, and other PublicLayout
   consumers are unaffected — they keep PublicLayout. *@
<footer class="editorial-footer">
    <div class="editorial-footer__content beeday-container">
        <button type="button" class="editorial-footer__back-to-top" @onclick="ScrollToTopAsync" aria-label="Back to top">
            @* ChevronDown rotated 180deg in CSS — the existing "Expand" chevron re-used as "up",
               avoiding a new icon asset for a single-direction affordance. *@
            <BeeDayIcon Name="BeeDayIconName.ChevronDown" Decorative="true" Class="editorial-footer__back-to-top-icon" />
        </button>
        <a class="editorial-footer__coffee" href="/buy-me-a-coffee">BUY ME A COFFEE</a>
        <p class="editorial-footer__copyright">© 2026 beeday. All rights reserved.</p>
    </div>
</footer>
